  "summary": "A marketplace where hosts set their own price per machine. Each figure is a floor - the median of the five cheapest asks on machines whose Stability and 30-Day Machine Uptime, as Octa.space prints them, are both 95% or more and which have at least one successful rental - withheld when too few qualify. Octa.space prints no verified badge; the thresholds are ours. The price is the machine's Total Cost as its card shows it, including the default 100 GB disk; traffic is billed per GB on top. Machines rented whole are a separate row; machines mixing two GPU models are not read.",
  "notes": "marketplace, server-rendered machine cards on cube.octa.computer/marketplace/compute, read sorted by total_price_usd asc, 100 a page, every page \"Showing N nodes\" calls for; trimmed floor of the 5 cheapest verified asks, withheld when the window cannot carry a floor (fewer than 3, or a median over 3x the cheapest); verified = Stability >= 95% and 30-Day Machine Uptime >= 95% and Success Rentals >= 1 (owner's rule of 2026-10-17); price = Total Cost (base + default 100 GB disk); single-GPU book = machines with one GPU line of 1x; multi-GPU book = one GPU line of 2+, per node; mixed machines not read; RTX 4000 (20 GB) not mapped (Ada or SFF Ada); links the sorted page the floor's machine stands on",
